--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/knowledge-rollback.md
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# Knowledge persistence rollback
+
+This boundary extraction deliberately does not change the `documents`, `embeddings`, or
+`deliveries` tables, their records, or the persistence implementation. Before any future
+persistence conversion, keep the current Active Record implementation available as the
+rollback point.
+
+If that conversion causes a regression, revert the conversion commit (or restore the
+Knowledge-owned models and queries from this revision), restart the application, and run
+the Knowledge characterization tests plus the `/documents` endpoint tests. The public
+`Knowledge::Catalog.list(tenant_id:)` contract is the stable seam: rollback work must
+preserve its published-only, id-ordered hashes and must not restore persistence access to
+Delivery. No data migration is required for this extraction, and no migration should be
+run as part of rolling it back.
